        "PMC8347531::web::013::3_5_annealing_treatment_on_the_al50ti20c"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Two-step-annealed alloys will have higher yield strength and higher uniform elongation than slow-cooled controls.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Conventionally slow-cooled eutectic HEAs have coarser lamellar morphologies, lack phase-specific recrystallization, and exhibit a typical strength–ductility trade-off.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Excessive annealing can coarsen the B2 phase or recrystallize both phases.",
